                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A.R.–N.C./17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-01-27T10:00:00-03:00">January 27, 1940—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. For the Under Secretary from Fenwick. Neutrality Committee seeking to
                    maintain its permanent character in spite of temporary absence of two members,
                    myself and Aguilar of Costa Rica. Hence brief recess after February 3.
                    Subcommittees will continue work until answer comes on the question of
                    jurisdiction when full Committee expected to meet. No necessity of making
                    provisional appointment at present. Will report on arrival February 11.
                    [Fenwick.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
